# Crypto Engine DISABLED — mainline sun8i-ce cannot drive the H713 CE (bench-
# proven 2026-07-23). Enabling it registers every algorithm, then each fails its
# known-answer self-test. Wiring the stock's 2nd interrupt (SPI 74) fixes task
# completion, but the CE then rejects mainline's task descriptors: ciphers report
# "address invalid", AES/SHA "algorithm not supported" — a different descriptor
# FORMAT (the vendor two-register-bank block), not an IRQ/clock/addressing gap.
# No CE TRNG either. Re-enabling needs descriptor-level RE of the vendor
# allwinner,sunxi-ce driver (source unavailable); the A53 has ARMv8 AES/SHA
# (software crypto ~2 GB/s, faster than this CE) so there is no benefit.
# See docs/status.md and docs/roadmap.md.
# Crypto Engine deliberately off, do not "complete" this. mainline sun8i-ce
# cannot drive the H713 CE: it uses a different task-descriptor format (the
# vendor two-bank block with 5-byte address fields), so every algorithm fails
# its known-answer test, and there is no TRNG. The A53s have the ARMv8 crypto
# extensions anyway, which are faster than this engine. The one thing the CE
# can do that software cannot -- read the RSSK efuse key for HDCP 1.4 -- needs
# a dedicated path, not this driver. See doku/114-plan-crypto-engine.md.
# CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_SUN8I_CE is not set
CONFIG_DMA_CMA=y
CONFIG_PRINTK_TIME=y
# No debugfs in the release kernel (Marco, 12.09.2026: "kein Debug im Release").
# What this closes: /sys/kernel/debug/cpu_comm/call, a prompt that sends any
# RPC by name straight to the display firmware, the writable tx_delay_* knobs
# next to it, and the write side of cpu_comm/watch, which claims callback
# slots. All of it sits under #ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS in cpu_comm_api.c with an
# empty #else, so the driver is untouched -- the switch alone does it. The
# read-only status files of hdmirx and cpu_comm go with it; h713-tv reports
# the missing path in "status" instead of failing, and "ctl rpc" says why it
# cannot. Nothing in the release rootfs reads debugfs. No enabled symbol
# selects DEBUG_FS, so "is not set" holds through olddefconfig (checked
# 12.09.2026 against lib/Kconfig.debug and friends). DYNAMIC_DEBUG only has a
# control file through debugfs; without it the pr_debug sites are dead weight.
# Development builds put both back with a fragment, not by editing this file.
# CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG is not set
# CONFIG_DEBUG_FS is not set
# Reboot-to-fastboot handoff over the RTC GP7 nvmem cell (see the RTC section and
# the reboot-mode node in sun50i-h713.dtsi). Replaces the earlier syscon window
# that overlapped the RTC register region.
CONFIG_NVMEM_REBOOT_MODE=y

# Messmodul fuer das Deskriptorformat der CE, ausdruecklich KEIN Ersatz fuer
# sun8i-ce: es registriert nichts beim Krypto-Kern, setzt genau einen Task im
# Vendorformat ab (AES-128, ECB oder CBC mit IV 0, Key-Select 0, Schluessel
# aus dem Speicher, 16 Byte, Ziel DRAM) und vergleicht mit dem FIPS-197-
# Vektor. Es fasst kein Geraeteschluesselmaterial und keine Schluesselsenke
# an. Es laedt beim Start ueber den Geraetebaum-Knoten, laeuft aber erst,
# wenn man es ueber /sys/kernel/debug/h713-ce-test/starten anstoesst. Nur als
# Modul (m), damit ein Messlauf eine Entscheidung bleibt. Siehe
# doku/114-plan-crypto-engine.md Paragraph 7 Schritt 3 und die README neben
# diesem Patch. Fuer ein Release kann die Zeile wieder raus.
CONFIG_H713_CE_TEST=m

# Magic SysRq in the shipping kernel, not only in the debug fragments (doku/124,
# after cstenger's 2026-08-22 finding). When the eMMC stops answering, reboot and
# systemctl are binaries on the dead filesystem and cannot run, and opening
# /dev/watchdog0 does nothing because systemd already holds and pets it.
# `echo b > /proc/sysrq-trigger` needs no filesystem, and neither does a UART
# BREAK (MAGIC_SYSRQ_SERIAL with the empty sequence arms it on BREAK alone).
# A hard lockup with every CPU spinning interrupts-off is still out of reach;
# this is for the softer wedge, the one that otherwise costs a trip to the plug.
CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ=y
CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ_SERIAL=y
CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ_DEFAULT_ENABLE=0x1
